  <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

  <div class="faq-item">
    <h3>How many pounds in a kilogram?</h3>
    <p>1 kilogram is equal to <strong>2.2046 pounds</strong>. This is the standard conversion factor used by the International System of Units (SI).</p>
  </div>

  <div class="faq-item">
    <h3>How do I convert kg to lbs manually?</h3>
    <p>Multiply the number of kilograms by <strong>2.2046</strong>. For example: <code>50 kg × 2.2046 = 110.23 lbs</code>. Use our converter above for instant results.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="faq-item">
    <h3>Why is 1 kg equal to 2.2046 lbs?</h3>
    <p>The kilogram is the SI base unit of mass, while the pound is an imperial/US customary unit. 1 kg = 2.20462262185 lbs is the internationally agreed conversion rate defined by the International Bureau of Weights and Measures.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="faq-item">
    <h3>Is this converter free to use?</h3>
    <p>Yes, this KG to LBS converter is completely free. No sign-up required, no limits on usage.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="faq-item">
    <h3>Which countries use kg vs lbs?</h3>
    <p>Kilograms are used in most countries worldwide (metric system). Pounds are primarily used in the <strong>United States</strong>, and to a lesser extent in the UK and Canada for body weight measurement.</p>
  </div>
